it has been heralded alternately as a  Google killer and the most important  general purpose technology since the  wheel or fire chat GPT is an AI powered  chatbot whose answers honestly feel  human but the very feature that makes it  seem almost magical also poses a  colossal problem because we don't really  know where its answers are coming from  foreign  let's start with the basics chat GPT is  built by openai a company that's backed  by Microsoft and it's more or less free  for anyone to use  it works by ingesting hundreds of  gigabytes of Text data on which it is  then trained to generate human-like  responses it's pretty mind-blowing this  is an essay that it wrote about Romeo  and Juliet this is some software code it  can even generate jokes that are almost  funny crucially it works differently  from Google it doesn't just quote  sources verbatim and present it to you  instead it works much the way a human  would if I've taken an undergraduate  course in say critical theory and  someone asked me about the German  sociologist teodor adorno I will dig  into the recesses of my memory and cough  up an answer I might not necessarily  know the exact source of that answer  some book or lecture for more than a  decade ago frankly my answer might not  be entirely accurate chat GPT is similar  it doesn't cite a source the way that a  responsible journalist or academic would  Google for all of its justifiable  criticism for the way that it scrapes  data from other websites and presents  them on its own platforms does at least  cite the source same with Wikipedia here  if you read an article that feels a  little bit sketchy you can click through  the source and find for yourself whether  you think it is accurate and Beyond just  checking the veracity of any information  The Source itself doesn't get any credit  that might be less incentive to post  things online if it's just being scraped  by some AI algorithm this is a bigger  issue with AI as a whole the very nature  of deep learning is such that often the  system itself doesn't know the source of  the information that it's presented  chat GPT is just a beta for the moment  maybe some of these issues can be fixed  but that's also why it's worth  discussing them right now  [Music]
 

